comments.body:
@Navid200 
I hope, I understood your question in the right way.
In my (many) case(s), the data comes from juggluco, which knows exactely when the session started, because it did it or receives the data directly from the sensor (when I use the original app to start the sensor and then take over with juggluco). The start time (and age) on the status page (in the working version) in xDrip was always exactly the original start time/age of the sensor for the past years. For "Libre patched" source that is. But the "Nighscout Follower" source which I just started to try out, showed the exact same date/age. Which is no wonder, as the data is still the same - coming from juggluco, just through another channel.

@PhilTU Another concern I have is that I don't have any knowledge of Libre.
Why we need another app is beyond me.  There are times this happens and I am aware of possibly similar scenarios in case of Dexcom.  So, if this is similar, we cannot do much about it. But, without knowing that, I have to know why it is we don't do what that other app does before I can attempt to change xDrip.

@tzachi-dar Do you have any ideas?
